  "purpose": {
    "classification": "DECLARED",
    "text": "ExecutionPartition and SafetyContract \u2014 the two orthogonal axes of operator placement.  These are separate types because they answer different questions: `ExecutionPartition` \u2014 WHERE does this operator run? `SafetyContract`     \u2014 WHAT does it guarantee about its runtime behaviour?  The compiler enforces: `SafetyContract::RealtimeSafe` is only valid on `AudioCallback` or `RealtimeCpu` partitions.  Any edge that crosses partition boundaries gets a compiler-inserted `Bridge`; no cross-partition calls on the hot path."
  },
